he rate remains mostly stable from quarter to quarter until a recession begins, causing it to fall. In this graph, we can observe the reallocation rate experiencing a permanent decrease following both the 2001 and 2008 recessions.\n\n Rate of job gains and job losses, third quarter 1992 to fourth quarter 2019\n\n| Quarter | Job gains | Job losses |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Q3 1992 | 8.2% | 7.5% |\n| Q4 1992 | 7.7 | 7.6 |\n| Q1 1993 | 8.1 | 7.7 |\n| Q2 1993 | 8.0 | 7.2 |\n| Q3 1993 | 8.3 | 7.1 |\n| Q4 1993 | 8.0 | 7.4 |\n| Q1 1994 | 8.2 | 7.5 |\n| Q2 1994 | 8.2 | 7.3 |\n| Q3 1994 | 8.5 | 7.1 |\n| Q4 1994 | 7.8 | 7.4 |\n| Q1 1995 | 8.3 | 7.4 |\n| Q2 1995 | 7.8 | 7.6 |\n| Q3 1995 | 8.3 | 7.3 |\n| Q4 1995 | 7.9 | 7.6 |\n| Q1 1996 | 8.3 | 7.7 |\n| Q2 1996 | 8.1 | 7.5 |\n| Q3 1996 | 8.3 | 7.5 |\n| Q4 1996 | 8.2 | 7.4 |\n| Q1 1997 | 8.4 | 7.5 |\n| Q2 1997 | 7.9 | 7.4 |\n| Q3 1997 | 8.4 | 7.5 |\n| Q4 1997 | 8.3 | 7.7 |\n| Q1 1998 | 8.5 | 7.7 |\n| Q2 1998 | 8.2 | 7.7 |\n| Q3 1998 | 8.1 | 7.4 |\n| Q4 1998 | 7.9 | 7.3 |\n| Q1 1999 | 8.2 | 7.8 |\n| Q2 1999 | 8.0 | 7.4 |\n| Q3 1999 | 8.0 | 7.4 |\n| Q4 1999 | 8.1 | 7.1 |\n| Q1 2000 | 8.3 | 7.4 |\n| Q2 2000 | 7.6 | 7.3 |\n| Q3 2000 | 7.7 | 7.4 |\n| Q4 2000 | 7.5 | 7.3 |\n| Q1 2001 | 7.9 | 7.8 |\n| Q2 2001 | 7.2 | 8.0 |\n| Q3 2001 | 7.1 | 8.1 |\n| Q4 2001 | 6.9 | 8.0 |\n| Q1 2002 | 7.6 | 7.6 |\n| Q2 2002 | 7.3 | 7.4 |\n| Q3 2002 | 7.1 | 7.2 |\n| Q4 2002 | 7.0 | 7.2 |\n| Q1 2003 | 7.1 | 7.4 |\n| Q2 2003 | 6.9 | 7.1 |\n| Q3 2003 | 7.0 | 6.7 |\n| Q4 2003 | 7.0 | 6.7 |\n| Q1 2004 | 7.3 | 6.8 |\n| Q2 2004 | 7.1 | 6.6 |\n| Q3 2004 | 7.1 | 6.8 |\n| Q4 2004 | 7.2 | 6.5 |\n| Q1 2005 | 7.1 | 6.6 |\n| Q2 2005 | 7.0 | 6.6 |\n| Q3 2005 | 7.3 | 6.5 |\n| Q4 2005 | 7.0 | 6.6 |\n| Q1 2006 | 7.0 | 6.2 |\n| Q2 2006 | 6.9 | 6.5 |\n| Q3 2006 | 6.7 | 6.6 |\n| Q4 2006 | 6.9 | 6.5 |\n| Q1 2007 | 6.9 | 6.4 |\n| Q2 2007 | 6.7 | 6.6 |\n| Q3 2007 | 6.4 | 6.6 |\n| Q4 2007 | 6.7 | 6.5 |\n| Q1 2008 | 6.4 | 6.5 |\n| Q2 2008 | 6.4 | 6.9 |\n| Q3 2008 | 6.1 | 7.0 |\n